---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>Yavuz Atilgan · Software Engineer</title>
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="Yavuz Atilgan, software engineering student. Front-end, back-end, full stack and AI. Looking for a graduation internship at BMW."
		/>
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<header>
			<nav aria-label="Main menu">
				<a class="logo" href="#top">Yavuz <b>A</b></a>
				<a href="#profile">Profile</a>
				<a href="#performance">Performance</a>
				<a href="#route">Route</a>
				<a href="#why-bmw">Why BMW</a>
				<a href="#contact">Contact</a>
			</nav>
		</header>

		<main id="top">
			<section class="intro">
				<p class="label">Software Engineer Student / Graduation Intern Candidate</p>
				<h1>Yavuz <span>Atilgan</span></h1>
				<p class="ondertitel">Sheer Programming Pleasure.</p>
				<p>
					Software engineering student from Rotterdam with a strong pull towards front-end,
					back-end, full stack and AI. Technically grounded, eager to learn and ambitious, and set
					on building software that actually adds value.
				</p>
				<p class="knoppen">
					<a class="knop" href="#profile">Start the engine</a>
					<a class="knop knop-rustig" href="#contact">Book a test drive</a>
				</p>
				<img class="intro-plaatje" src="/afbeeldingen/dashboard.svg" alt="" width="300" height="210" />

				<dl class="feiten">
					<div>
						<dt>Engine</dt>
						<dd>Full stack <small>JS · TS · PHP · Java</small></dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Drivetrain</dt>
						<dd>xDrive <small>front + back end + AI</small></dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Programme</dt>
						<dd>HBO SD <small>Hogeschool Rotterdam</small></dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Target</dt>
						<dd>BMW Group <small>graduation internship</small></dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</section>

			<section id="profile">
				<p class="label">01 / Driver profile</p>
				<h2>The engineer behind the wheel</h2>

				<div class="twee-kolommen">
					<article>
						<p class="groot">
							Motivated software engineering student with a strong interest in front-end,
							back-end, full stack development and AI.
						</p>
						<p>
							Technically grounded, eager to learn and ambitious. I want to build innovative,
							modern software solutions that add value and make an impact. In practice that means
							caring about the things nobody sees in a demo: error handling, tests, and code the
							next engineer can read without a manual.
						</p>
						<p>
							I work across the whole stack. HTML, SCSS, TypeScript and React on the front, PHP,
							Node.js, Java and Python behind it, SQL underneath, and Kotlin or Swift when it has
							to run in someone's hand. Currently completing HBO Software Developer at Hogeschool
							Rotterdam and looking for the graduation internship that pushes me hardest.
						</p>
						<p>
							The other half of me is a car person. Getting to write software for the company
							that builds the machines I have read about for years is not just an application. It
							is the obvious destination.
						</p>
						<ul class="woorden">
							<li>Analytical</li>
							<li>Eager to learn</li>
							<li>Ambitious</li>
							<li>Problem-solving</li>
							<li>Team player</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<aside class="datakaart">
						<h3>Technical data</h3>
						<table>
							<tbody>
								<tr><th>Model</th><td>Yavuz Atilgan</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Series</th><td>Software Engineer Student</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Status</th><td>Available for internship</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Front</th><td>HTML · SCSS · TypeScript · React</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Back</th><td>PHP · Node.js · Java · Python</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Mobile</th><td>Kotlin · Swift</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Target</th><td class="blauw">BMW Group</td></tr>
							</tbody>
						</table>

						<h3>Languages</h3>
						<table>
							<tbody>
								<tr><th>Dutch</th><td>Fluent</td></tr>
								<tr><th>English</th><td>Fluent</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Turkish</th><td>Fluent</td></tr>
								<tr><th>Italian</th><td>Basic</td></tr>
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</aside>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="performance">
				<p class="label">02 / Performance</p>
				<h2>Power output</h2>
				<p>Telemetry per discipline. Redline at 8.000 rpm.</p>

				<ul class="meters">
					<li>
						<h3>JavaScript / TypeScript <small>Daily driver</small></h3>
						<p class="meter"><span style="width: 80%"></span></p>
						<p class="rpm">8.0 <small>rpm × 1000</small></p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>React / SCSS <small>Front-end</small></h3>
						<p class="meter"><span style="width: 85%"></span></p>
						<p class="rpm">8.5 <small>rpm × 1000</small></p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>PHP / Node.js <small>Back-end</small></h3>
						<p class="meter"><span style="width: 75%"></span></p>
						<p class="rpm">7.5 <small>rpm × 1000</small></p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Java / Python <small>OOP &amp; AI</small></h3>
						<p class="meter"><span style="width: 80%"></span></p>
						<p class="rpm">8.0 <small>rpm × 1000</small></p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>SQL / PhpMyAdmin <small>Data</small></h3>
						<p class="meter"><span style="width: 75%"></span></p>
						<p class="rpm">7.5 <small>rpm × 1000</small></p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Kotlin / Swift <small>Android &amp; iOS</small></h3>
						<p class="meter"><span style="width: 70%"></span></p>
						<p class="rpm">7.0 <small>rpm × 1000</small></p>
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Full toolbox</h3>
				<ul class="woorden">
					<li>HTML</li>
					<li>CSS</li>
					<li>SCSS</li>
					<li>JavaScript</li>
					<li>TypeScript</li>
					<li>React</li>
					<li>Node.js</li>
					<li>PHP</li>
					<li>Java</li>
					<li>Python</li>
					<li>SQL</li>
					<li>PhpMyAdmin</li>
					<li>Kotlin</li>
					<li>Swift</li>
					<li>Git</li>
					<li>GitHub</li>
					<li>Azure DevOps</li>
					<li>Linux</li>
					<li>Android</li>
					<li>iOS</li>
					<li>AI</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="route">
				<p class="label">03 / The route so far</p>
				<h2>Navigation history</h2>

				<ol class="tijdlijn">
					<li>
						<p class="wanneer">Next</p>
						<h3>Graduation internship <small>Destination</small></h3>
						<p>
							The final stage of my degree: a graduation internship where I can ship production
							software inside a real engineering culture, preferably one that measures things in
							Nm and ms.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p class="wanneer">Now</p>
						<h3>HBO Software Developer</h3>
						<p>
							Hogeschool Rotterdam. Full stack development, software architecture and working in
							Scrum teams: the programme I am completing now.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p class="wanneer">HBO</p>
						<h3>Informatica, 2 years</h3>
						<p>
							Hogeschool Rotterdam. Two years of computer science: algorithms, databases,
							networking and the theory underneath everything I build now.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p class="wanneer">MBO</p>
						<h3>Software Developer</h3>
						<p>
							GLR Grafisch Lyceum Rotterdam. Where the foundation was laid: my first real
							codebases, first clients and the moment I realised debugging is genuinely fun.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section id="why-bmw">
				<p class="label">04 / Destination</p>
				<h2>Why BMW</h2>
				<p class="groot">
					Not because it is a famous logo. Because of how the cars are engineered.
				</p>

				<ul class="kaarten">
					<li>
						<p class="nummer">01</p>
						<h3>Engineering without compromise</h3>
						<p>
							A near 50:50 weight distribution is not a marketing line, it is a decision that
							costs money and effort. That is exactly the standard I want to hold my code to: do it
							properly, even when nobody would notice the shortcut.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p class="nummer">02</p>
						<h3>Software is the new drivetrain</h3>
						<p>
							Modern BMWs run on millions of lines of code: driver assistance, electrification,
							connected services, over-the-air updates. This is the most exciting time in history
							to be a software engineer in automotive, and I want to be in that room.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p class="nummer">03</p>
						<h3>Sheer Driving Pleasure, in code</h3>
						<p>
							The best software feels like the best cars: responsive, predictable and quietly
							confident. I obsess over that feeling (latency, motion, feedback) because it is the
							difference between a tool people use and one they enjoy.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ul>

				<blockquote class="uitgelicht">
					<p>If they say it is impossible, it is impossible for them, not for me.</p>
					<footer>Yavuz Atilgan</footer>
				</blockquote>
			</section>

			<section id="contact">
				<p class="label">05 / Contact</p>
				<h2>Let us talk about the internship.</h2>
				<p class="groot">
					Available for a graduation internship. CV, references and code samples on request.
				</p>
				<ul class="contact">
					<li>
						<span>E-mail</span>
						<a href="mailto:yavuzatilgan7@gmail.com">yavuzatilgan7@gmail.com</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span>GitHub</span>
						<a href="https://github.com/Yavuz-1073705">github.com/Yavuz-1073705</a>
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					<a class="knop" href="mailto:yavuzatilgan7@gmail.com?subject=Graduation%20internship">Send a message</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>

		<footer>
			<p class="logo">Yavuz <b>A</b></p>
			<p>Driven by code. Fueled by <b>BMW</b>.</p>
			<p>Built with Astro, HTML and CSS.</p>
			<p class="klein">
				Independent personal portfolio. Not affiliated with, endorsed by or produced by BMW AG. All
				trademarks belong to their respective owners.
			</p>
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>
